## Want to learn how to play OGFN with ATLAS?

Download **ATLAS Link** launcher and **ATLAS Backend** from the following GitHub links (open source and safe):
> 1. https://github.com/cipherfps/ATLAS-Link/releases/
> 2. https://github.com/cipherfps/ATLAS-Backend/releases/
-# Note for Trickshotters:
> - This backend is how you can have **MODIFIED** item properties with CurveTables and Straight Bloom (Ex. Super Shockwave/Flintknock, Straight Bullet, etc.):
> - ATLAS Backend allows you to change the values of those items directly on the menu
> - https://github.com/cipherfps/ATLAS-Backend
> - Looking for a specific CurveTable that is not listed? Visit the following Github page:
> - https://github.com/Ralzify/lawin-repo/blob/main/Curve%20Tables.md

Download a **Fortnite Version** or **Build** you'd like to play on from either one of these sites (ATLAS supports v1.7.2-30.00):
> - https://builds.fortforge.dev/builds (Clean UI/Easy to Navigate)
> - https://github.com/Helix-Dev-Q/fortnite-builds-archive (Ctrl + F to serach for build)
> - Download <#1503461822961811727> and extract your Fortnite build

How to **LAUNCH/START** your game:
> - Open ATLAS Link, import your build if you haven't already (Make sure the **folder** you select contains both `FortniteGame and Engine`)
> - Start your Backend if not already started
> - Click `Launch` and make sure to continue with  `Start game server`
> - You should see a GUI menu start up along with the game, that is your game server
> - To enter the game wait till the GUI says `Status: Joinable!` as that indicates your server is ready
> - Click on your Fortnite game and press the (F8) or (~) key, you should see a terminal open
> - Type the following command to enter your game: `open 127.0.0.1`

How to use **COMMANDS** and **OBTAIN** weapons or items:
> - Go to this pastebin that contains most commands and weapon/consumable IDs for all versions:
> - https://pastebin.com/4pmMgegz
> - (Ctrl + F) to search for an item
> - Go to your Fortnite game and click (F8) or (~) key to open the terminal
> - Paste the command and you should recieve your item!

Most useful **COMMANDS**:
> - `cheat s [type anything here]` to save a waypoint at your pawns location!
> - `cheat w [what you typed earlier]`  to teleport to a specific waypoint!
> - `cheat destroyall drop` to destroy all supply drops that have spawned
> - `cheat bot [amount]` to spawn a bot! (If you want AIs that move around visit this channel: https://discord.com/channels/1469866169635962884/1469876652388515986)
> - `cheat startaircraft` to start the bus without the GUI, sometimes works better and doesn't crash
> - Do `cheat help` to view the rest of the command list in game







## EXTENDED GUIDE...
How to launch **MULTIPLE CLIENTS**:
> - Go to the ATLAS Link library menu
> - Click on the `...` button to open Launch Options
> - Toggle on `Multi-Client Launching` and click `Save`
> - Launch your first client, this will launch with your username
> - Once that game finishes loading up, launch your second client
> - Make sure to name your second client a different username
> - Type the following command on both clients to enter your game: `open 127.0.0.1`
-# Note for Trickshotters:
> - Second clients are useful for the Infinite Render option included in the gameserver/backend 
> - This feature allows your sniper bullet projectile to travel infinitely

How to **PLAY** with **FRIENDS**:
> - Download the program below to allow others to connect to your matches
> - https://www.radmin-vpn.com/
> - Open Radmin, navigate to the tabs at the top and click `System > Firewall Exceptions > Allow All Apps`
> - Now you can either create a network or join your friends network
> - Navigate to `Network` and click `Create Network` or `Join Network`
> - Once created share your username and password to others to allow their connection
> - Afterward, whoever is hosting, make sure to copy their randomly **generated IP**
> -----------------------------------------
> - **If you are using ATLAS Backend and want to have seperate skins:**
> - Open ATLAS Link
> - Navigate to `Backend` and switch `Local` to `Remote`
> - Then put the host's IP in the `Host` box
> - Afterward click `Check Backend`
> - If it returns `Backend reachable` continue to the next step
> -# Note: The host stays on Local
> -----------------------------------------
> - Launch your Fortnite and click `Start Server`
> - Click on your Fortnite game and press the (F8) or (~) key, you should see a terminal open
> - Type the following command to enter your game: `open [paste IP here]`
> **Troubleshooting:**
> - If you do not have the firewall option this means a third-party application/antivirus may be interfering with the firewall
> - Allowing all Apps just allows a smoother or easier time connecting the player(s) and the host, although it is completely optional
